                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ottoman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                        "entry_id": "1284b143-59cc-32c6-87c6-0351f829e43f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Archaic form of Osman, the name borne by",
                                            "Osman I (d. 1323/4), founder of the Ottoman Empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8b93f76-2941-461a-b9d6-b733d5a44d3a",
                                                "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                                "text": "In the beginning of this yere Sulton Solyman Pac called yͤ great Turke which was but the. viii. of the ligne of Ottoman, the firſt that toke vpō hym to be a great capitain or ruler […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8568f07e-05a7-4f8b-af58-ac7aafb9258c",
                                                "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                                "text": "Ottoman the firſte Emperour of this Turkiſhe nation, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d971aee4-c2f4-43b6-95e4-adc76728a49c",
                                                "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                                "text": "In the Firſt Place are Conditores Imperiorum; Founders of States, and Common-Wealths: Such as were Romulus, Cyrus, Cæſar, Ottoman, Iſmael."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d428227-4ad6-477d-9d40-f9d59a0d2619",
                                                "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                                "text": "It is unqueſtionable, that about the year 1300 upon Aladin’s Death, Ottoman was an abſolute Soveraign […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c60258c9-93b5-4ad5-9f3f-d246dce9b13c",
                                                "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                                "text": "OTTOMAN the Son of Ethrogul the Son of Solyman (who was drove out of Perſia by the Tartars) was about A.D. 1290 ſaluted with the Title of Governor of the Oguzian Turks in Aſia […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba0e7497-dd2f-4add-9ece-f2c00460ecfe",
                                                "sense_id": "561c4fc6-ecb6-31ad-a4a8-7a7de774f205",
                                                "text": "Ottoman, notwithſtanding this Succeſs, thought fit to agree to a Truce with the Chriſtians […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b89dd61-a59a-3b28-a7cb-beceb875c42e",
                                        "entry_id": "1284b143-59cc-32c6-87c6-0351f829e43f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Archaic form of Osman, the name borne by",
                                            "Osman II (1604–1622), sultan of the Ottoman Empire from 1618 until his death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65559f63-ad24-453a-b55f-817ae4e04aee",
                                                "sense_id": "7b89dd61-a59a-3b28-a7cb-beceb875c42e",
                                                "text": "And in the year 1618. (when Ottoman the ſecond (who ſucceeded his Uncle Muſtapha) was unſuccessful in his war againſt Poland, and was therefore ſlain by his Janizaries) […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1851c5cb-509d-4539-8936-dc519739d2d2",
                                                "sense_id": "7b89dd61-a59a-3b28-a7cb-beceb875c42e",
                                                "text": "After theſe reign'd […] Ottoman II. ſtrangled by the Janizaries, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51b6542d-0042-468b-8db8-b6a7aa85eb48",
                                                "sense_id": "7b89dd61-a59a-3b28-a7cb-beceb875c42e",
                                                "text": "Oſman, or Ottoman II, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d057dbd5-bba3-3ad4-a843-859aa5de1dcd",
                                        "entry_id": "1284b143-59cc-32c6-87c6-0351f829e43f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Archaic form of Osman, the name borne by",
                                            "Osman III (1699–1757), sultan of the Ottoman Empire from 1754 until his death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29c7704e-2bd9-4775-854f-1d7968d0aa23",
                                                "sense_id": "d057dbd5-bba3-3ad4-a843-859aa5de1dcd",
                                                "text": "Ottoman III."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8026367-a066-474f-95ba-5e2ca800f30d",
                                                "sense_id": "d057dbd5-bba3-3ad4-a843-859aa5de1dcd",
                                                "text": "[…] the reign of Ottoman III (reigned 1754–57) after the death of Mahmut I."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ottoman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "748d4aaa-a1bd-3304-baf8-229b752c3445",
                                        "entry_id": "cdc81c71-089a-39cc-8778-98e2ba57c745",
