                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A citizen of the Ottoman Empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "712560d0-138d-4679-9e06-faefdbf31c1f",
                                                "sense_id": "108020da-990a-3be3-9d30-5010b6e7f6ec",
                                                "text": "Nearly 250,000 Ottomans of various military ranks were taken captive by the Allied forces during World War I, which was referred to in Turkish variously as Büyük Harp, Cihan Harbi and Harb-i Umumi (or simply Seferberlik among the older generation of Turks) until World War II."
                                            }
